# Bastion Pass Release Notes

## 1.0.0 (16 May 2026)
* Update README.md file
* Rename PyPass to Bastion Pass
* Update Buy me a Coffee link to new username
* Fix background server so user can now login

## 1.0.0 (06 June 2026)
* Started fixing migration server

## 1.0.0 (07 June 2026)
* Set up framework for data migration into background server

## 1.0.0 (12 June 2026)
* Start adding sending data functionality into background server
* Simplify add_to_screen function
* Temporarily disable backup phrase creation

## 1.0.0 (04 July 2026)
* Fix server event loop being blocked, triggering constant warning in console

## 1.0.0 (08 July 2026)
* Replaced httpx and debug server with message listener inside of app
* Fix background server so app can start it on startup, and doesn't block app thread

## 1.0.0 (09 July 2026)
* Layout most of the UI for importing passwords from files
* Start working on the import passwords from files functionality

## 1.0.0 (10 July 2026)
* Work on functionality for importing passwords from files

## 1.0.0 (11 July 2026)
* Finish up functionality for importing passwords from files
* Fix create backup phrase for desktop OS's, so now the backup phrase is automatically written to the selected file
* Remove CHANGELOG.md from .gitignore

## 1.0.0 (29 July 2026)
* Fix layout so content is now centered
* Remove duplicate definition of home widgets
* Work on trying to get background server to start

## 1.0.0 (30 July 2026)
* Add send data functionality
* Start working on connection refused error handling

## 1.0.0 (31 July 2026)
* Switch messages from server to app from strings to dictionaries
* Add error handling for connection errors

## 1.0.0 (08 August 2026)
* Work on receiving device deoffset data functionality
* Add new function to utilities to help with deoffseting offset strings
* Fix usernames, passwords, keys, and ivs not being reset between username offset

## 1.0.0 (18 August 2026)
* Add command to manually trigger offset and deoffset functions

## 1.0.0 (19 August 2026)
* Work on move offset function to offset string instead of offset user data
* Add missing comma between '-' and '!' characters
* Get receiving data functionality mostly working
* Fix app crashing on Ubuntu

## 1.0.0 (26 August 2026)
* Fix data migration so if service and username already exists on receiving device, existing password will be overwritten
* Got data migration working from pypass to bastion pass except on android

## 1.0.0 (27 August 2026)
* Fix saved legacy received data to wrong file
* Add file cleanup after receiving data